	<key>CFBundleVersion</key>
	<string>11</string>
	<key>LSRequiresIPhoneOS</key>
	<true/>
	<key>NSCameraUsageDescription</key>
	<string>SkateHubba uses the camera to record a trick and to take a profile photo. The camera stays on only while you are recording or taking that photo.</string>
	<key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
	<string>SkateHubba uses the microphone only while you are recording a trick, so the clip has sound.</string>
	<key>NSPhotoLibraryUsageDescription</key>
	<string>SkateHubba opens your photo library only when you choose something from it: a profile photo or banner, or a skate video to upload or edit in the clip editor.</string>
	<key>NSPhotoLibraryAddUsageDescription</key>
	<string>SkateHubba can save a profile photo you choose to keep, and save full-quality clips you export from the clip editor to your camera roll.</string>
	<key>NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription</key>
	<string>SkateHubba uses your location only while you are using the app, to show skate spots near you and to confirm you are at a spot when you check in. Your exact location is never shown to other skaters.</string>
